# customer-template-dro

Full guidance: `.cursor/skills/rlm-customer-demo-dro/SKILL.md`.

## Query step groups before writing ProductFulfillmentScenario.csv

```bash
sf data query -q "SELECT Id, Name FROM FulfillmentStepDefinitionGroup" --target-org <alias>
```

Group names are **org-specific**. "Order Processing" often does not exist. When the name
does not match, SFDMU silently sets `FulfillmentStepDefnGroupId = null` — no error, and the
Fulfillment tab stays empty.

Typical mapping (verify per org): Finance to `Finance`; services delivery to `Services`;
subscription provisioning to `Provisioning & Activation`; platform to `Platform`; usage
metering to `Usage Provisioning & Activation`.

## Scope

This overlay adds `ProductFulfillmentDecompRule`, `ProductFulfillmentScenario`, and a
`Product2.DecompositionScope` Update only. Step groups, step definitions, workspaces, and
jeopardy rules come from `prepare_dro` and must already exist, along with `QB-DRO-BILL` and
`QB-DRO-PROJ`.

`DecompositionScope` is `Bundle` on bundle parents, `OrderLineItem` on everything else.

## Two object sets

Set 1: `Product2` + `FulfillmentStepDefinitionGroup` as `Readonly`, plus PFDR and PFS
Upserts. Set 2: `Product2` Update scoped to customer SKUs. This avoids two `Product2`
entries in one object set.

PFDR and PFS use `Upsert` on `externalId: Name`, so re-runs are idempotent.

## Known non-issues

`ExecuteOnRuleId` and `ScenarioRuleId` are null on all records in most orgs — normal.
Decomposition may require a manual **Submit Orchestration Request** click on the order's
Fulfillment tab after activation.
